From: 主理-75 <主理-75@local>
Subject: [PATCH] ipsupport.cpp: keep musl sockaddr_storage when netlink is used

On OHOS compiling this file dies with
  linux/socket.h:23:8: error: redefinition of 'sockaddr_storage'
  sys/socket.h:377:8: note: previous definition is here
The include order is already correct (sys/socket.h line 26, kernel headers
29-31), but the OHOS sysroot ships a kernel-generated linux/socket.h that
defines the struct unconditionally -- the documented OHOS header inconsistency
of knowledge/graph/E091.kv (root_cause line 17, rec_approach define-guard
line 28). Rename the kernel variant only while its headers are pulled in, then
restore the name: the netlink API used here never touches that struct, and the
guard is __OHOS__-only inside an existing HAVE_LINUX_NETLINK block, so no other
platform changes.

--- a/src/libserver/ipsupport.cpp
+++ b/src/libserver/ipsupport.cpp
@@ -27,8 +27,14 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 #ifdef HAVE_LINUX_NETLINK
 #include <asm/types.h>
+#ifdef __OHOS__
+#define sockaddr_storage __linux_sockaddr_storage
+#endif
 #include <linux/netlink.h>
 #include <linux/rtnetlink.h>
+#ifdef __OHOS__
+#undef sockaddr_storage
+#endif
 #endif
 #ifdef HAVE_WINDOWS_IPHELPER
 #define Array XArray
